(optional)\n   - Recap what was learned\n   - Reinforce the learning objectives\n   - Celebrate the achievement\n\n9. **Next steps** section\n   - Related tutorials to explore\n   - Features to try next\n   - Ways to build on what they've learned\n\n10. **Related pages** section\n    - Links to how-to guides\n    - Links to reference documentation\n    - Links to related tutorials\n\n## Style Requirements\n\n- **Tone**: Friendly, encouraging, supportive\n- **Tense**: Present tense\n- **Voice**: Active voice, guide the learner\n- **Pronouns**: \"You\", \"your\", \"we\" (when collaborative)\n- **Focus**: Progressive learning, building skills step-by-step\n- **Guidance**: Explain WHY things work, not just HOW\n\n## Content Guidelines\n\n- Start simple, build complexity gradually\n- Assume users are new to the feature or workflow\n- Provide encouragement and context\n- Use realistic, relatable examples\n- Each step should build on previous steps\n- Include checkpoints so users know they're on track\n- Be complete: users shouldn't need to jump to other docs\n- Use clear, descriptive headings for each section\n- Balance between guidance and independence\n\n## Formatting Rules\n\n- Use Markdown headers: # (title), ## (sections), ### (subsections)\n- Use numbered lists for procedures\n- Use bulleted lists for options, prerequisites, objectives\n- Use code blocks with language specification: ```bash, ```json, ```yaml\n- Use bold (**text**) for UI elements and important terms\n- Use backticks for commands, files, values: `like_this`\n- Include screenshots or diagrams if they clarify complex UI\n- Use admonitions sparingly for important notes or tips\n\n## Word Choice\n\n✓ Use: create, build, configure, set up, enable, understand, explore\n✗ Avoid: easy, simple, just, click (unless exact mouse action), will, must, should\n\n## Output\n\nGenerate the complete tutorial in Markdown format.\n- Include all required sections\n- Start with frontmatter (if needed)\n- Make it progressive and learner-friendly\n- Include realistic examples\n- Include verification checkpoints\n- Include helpful explanations\n- No placeholder text\n- Ready to publish\n- Test-ready (users should be able to follow start to finish)\n\nNow create the tutorial."
