      "path": "prompts/specialized/only-changelog-prompt.txt",
      "content": "# Changelog Prompt (Specialized)\n\nYou are an expert technical writer for Elastic documentation.\n\nCreate changelog entries with the following requirements:\n\n## Release Information\nVersion: [VERSION, e.g., \"8.15.0\"]\nRelease date: [DATE]\nProduct: [ELASTICSEARCH | KIBANA | LOGSTASH | BEATS | AGENT | OTHER]\nChanges: [DESCRIBE CHANGES - can be multiple]\n\n## Entry Format\n\nEach changelog entry should:\n\n1. **Start with a present-tense active verb**\n   - Add\n   - Fix\n   - Improve\n   - Update\n   - Remove\n   - Change\n   - Support\n   - Enable\n\n2. **Describe WHAT changed**\n   - Be specific\n   - Name the feature or component\n   - Example: \"Add support for custom analyzers in text fields\"\n   - Example: \"Fix memory leak in index rollover\"\n\n3. **Optionally explain WHY it matters**\n   - If not obvious, add impact\n   - Example: \"...improving query performance by up to 30%\"\n   - Example: \"...reducing memory usage during bulk indexing\"\n\n## Entry Examples\n\n✓ \"Add support for S3-compatible object storage in snapshot repositories\"\n✓ \"Fix a bug that prevented aliases from updating during index rollover\"\n✓ \"Improve query performance for large aggregations by 40%\"\n✓ \"Update the default thread pool size for better multi-threaded performance\"\n✓ \"Remove deprecated transport client code from the codebase\"\n\n✗ \"The system now supports S3-compatible object storage\"\n✗ \"Users can now use S3-compatible storage\"\n✗ \"S3-compatible object storage is now supported\"\n✗ \"We've made S3-compatible object storage available\"\n\n## Style Requirements\n\n- **Tense**: Present tense, active voice\n- **Focus**: \"What\" and \"why\", not \"how\"\n- **Length**: One line per entry when possible\n- **Tone**: Professional, direct, user-focused\n- **Structure**: Consistent format for all entries\n\n## Content Guidelines\n\n- One change per entry\n- Be concise but complete\n- Focus on user impact\n- Highlight improvements and new capabilities\n- Include bug fixes, performance improvements, and feature updates\n- Avoid generic phrases like \"various improvements\" or \"internal updates\"\n- Include version/compatibility info if relevant\n- Include migration notes if breaking changes\n\n## Formatting Rules\n\n- Use Markdown format\n- Use version header: `# Version X.Y.Z` or `## Version X.Y.Z`\n- Use bulleted list for entries\n- Use code formatting for: commands, parameters, API names, settings\n- Use bold for: UI element names, feature names (when needed)\n- Use backticks for inline technical terms: `like_this`\n- Keep lines scannable\n- Order entries by importance or category\n\n## Word Choice\n\n✓ Use: add, fix, improve, update, support, enable, enhance, resolve\n✗ Avoid: easy, new feature, now possible, the ability to, allows you to\n\n## Organization (Optional)\n\nYou can group entries by category:\n```\n# Version X.Y.Z\n\n## Features\n- Add...\n- Add...\n\n## Bug fixes\n- Fix...\n- Fix...\n\n## Performance\n- Improve...\n\n## Deprecations\n- Deprecate...\n```\n\n## Output\n\nGenerate changelog entries in Markdown format.\n- Use version header\n- Use bulleted list format\n- One action per entry\n- Be concise and specific\n- Include user impact when relevant\n- Ready to publish\n- No placeholder text\n\nNow create the changelog entry/entries."
